course: dictionary
lesson: 5691
title: Old names, new meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some illnesses have old names that sound strange today. Lockjaw is an old everyday name for tetanus. «Do not pick up a sharp rusty nail with bare hands; tell a grown-up, and tell them if it cut you, because rusty cuts can cause tetanus (also called lockjaw, an illness that makes the muscles go stiff; a doctor can stop it).» The words in brackets are the clue: "also called" tells you lockjaw is another name for the same illness.
explain: Use the words around a new word to work out its meaning. Lock means something stays shut tight, and jaw is the part of your face that moves when you open your mouth. Put them together and you can guess that the illness locks the jaw. Then check your guess by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
explain: Lockjaw has a second meaning: a tight cramp in the jaw muscles, so the mouth will not open properly. Which meaning fits depends on the words around it. If the sentence is about germs and wounds, it means the illness.
fact: Lockjaw is an old everyday name for tetanus.
fact: Tetanus is a serious illness caused by germs getting into a wound, which makes muscles go stiff.
fact: Germs can get into a deep cut from a rusty nail or dirty soil.
fact: A tetanus jab, also called a vaccine, protects you against tetanus.
fact: If you cut yourself on something rusty or dirty, tell a grown-up, because a doctor can stop tetanus.
exercise: What can a deep cut from a rusty nail let into your body? | Music | *Germs that can cause tetanus | Sunshine | Cold air
exercise: «...tetanus (also called lockjaw...)» What does lockjaw mean here? | A cold in the nose | A cut that stops bleeding | A type of rusty nail | *Another name for tetanus, an illness that makes the muscles go stiff
exercise: Which of these protects you against tetanus? | *A tetanus jab | A rusty nail | A sticking plaster | A cool drink
test: What does tetanus make your muscles do? | *Go stiff | Grow faster | Sing loudly | Go floppy and weak
test: Why should you tell a grown-up if a rusty nail cuts you? | Because the nail is shiny | *Because germs could get in and cause tetanus | Because nails are sharp to touch | Because the cut looks red
exam: Which phrase means having a tetanus vaccine? | Dry your jaw | *A tetanus jab | Eat lockjaw | Lock the door
